  "dbErrorTitle": "Impossible d'ouvrir vos données",
  "@dbErrorTitle": {
    "description": "Title of the screen shown when the encrypted database cannot be opened. States the fact, never the cause: a keystore wipe, a device restore, a corrupted file and an OEM security reset all arrive as the same exception, and a guessed cause sends the driver off to fix something that is not broken. Never names encryption, keys or databases — that is our vocabulary, not his."
  },
  "dbErrorStillTrue": "Vos colis et le travail d'aujourd'hui ne sont pas perdus. L'entreprise garde sa propre trace du lot. Ce qui manque, c'est la copie de l'application — pas votre argent.",
  "@dbErrorStillTrue": {
    "description": "The most important string on this screen, and the reason it is long. It is the difference between a driver who continues his day and one who stops. Three jobs: the parcels in his hand are still real, the company still holds its own record of the batch, and what was lost is the app's copy of the history rather than his work or his money. Do not shorten by dropping a clause; split into more sentences instead."
  },
  "dbErrorReconcile": "Avant toute autre chose, comparez l'argent encaissé aujourd'hui avec le bordereau de l'entreprise.",
  "@dbErrorReconcile": {
    "description": "TODO(bordereau): the Arabic rendering of \"bordereau\" is unresolved. Shipping as وصل الشركة, which is understandable and safe, but this is trade vocabulary and belongs to a real manifest rather than to a guess. If drivers say البوردورو, that is the answer. Resolved by the same trip that settles the wilaya structure and the failure-reason taxonomy. Emphasised, and deliberately NOT a numbered troubleshooting step. It fixes nothing, so listing it after 'retry' would read as what you do once the other steps fail. It is what the driver does first, and it stays true even if retry succeeds: if his money records are gone, the company's bordereau is the surviving source."
  },
  "dbErrorStep1": "Réessayez.",
  "@dbErrorStep1": {
    "description": "First troubleshooting step. Least destructive first."
  },
  "dbErrorStep2": "Redémarrez le téléphone, puis réessayez.",
  "@dbErrorStep2": {
    "description": "Second troubleshooting step."
  },
  "dbErrorRetry": "Réessayer",
  "@dbErrorRetry": {
    "description": "The only action visible at first view. Re-attempts the database open, which is worth keeping because a transient keystore failure can clear on relaunch — the one case where this screen is recoverable."
  },
  "dbErrorWhyLabel": "Pourquoi ?",
  "@dbErrorWhyLabel": {
    "description": "Expands the secondary disclosure below."
  },
  "dbErrorWhyBody": "Cela peut arriver après la restauration d'un téléphone depuis une sauvegarde, ou après le passage à un nouvel appareil : les données peuvent être copiées, mais pas ce qui permet de les ouvrir.",
  "@dbErrorWhyBody": {
    "description": "Phrased as 'this can happen after', never 'this happened because'. We cannot determine the cause, and a wrong explanation on the worst day costs more trust than no explanation."
  },
  "dbErrorOtherOptions": "Autres options",
  "@dbErrorOtherOptions": {
    "description": "Secondary path on the failure screen, leading to the destructive reset. Never a peer of the retry button: a driver who has just read that his data will not open must not be one panicked tap from destroying it."
  },
  "dbErrorResetFailed": "La réinitialisation ne s'est pas terminée.",
  "@dbErrorResetFailed": {
    "description": "Shown on the failure screen when a reset attempt did not complete. Deliberately says nothing about whether the data survived — the delete may have succeeded before the key regeneration failed, so any claim either way could be false. It is one line added to the existing screen rather than a new error state: the driver has now had two things fail, and composing a second error on top of the first makes the screen read as though the app is confused about which."
  },
  "resetTitle": "Effacer les données et recommencer",
  "@resetTitle": {
    "description": "Title of the first reset step. Names the action plainly — not 'Réinitialiser', which sounds reversible."
  },
  "resetLosesIntro": "Ceci supprime définitivement ce que l'application a enregistré sur ce téléphone :",
  "@resetLosesIntro": {
    "description": "Introduces the loss list. Categories rather than counts, because the database is unreadable and we cannot count what is in it."
  },
  "resetLosesDeliveries": "les livraisons et leur historique",
  "@resetLosesDeliveries": {
    "description": "First loss category."
  },
  "resetLosesCustomers": "les clients et leurs adresses enregistrées",
  "@resetLosesCustomers": {
    "description": "Second loss category. 'Adresses enregistrées' covers the learned pins, which are the most expensive thing to rebuild."
  },
  "resetLosesMoney": "les encaissements et les règlements",
  "@resetLosesMoney": {
    "description": "Third loss category, and the one with financial consequence."
  },
  "resetIrreversible": "Rien de tout cela ne peut être récupéré.",
  "@resetIrreversible": {
    "description": "Stated as its own sentence. No backup exists, and promising recovery would be a lie."
  },
  "resetReconcileFirst": "Si ce n'est pas déjà fait, comparez d'abord l'argent encaissé avec le bordereau de l'entreprise. C'est le dernier moment pour le faire.",
  "@resetReconcileFirst": {
    "description": "Repeats the reconcile instruction from the failure screen, because this is genuinely the last moment it is useful. TODO(bordereau): see the note on dbErrorReconcile."
  },
  "resetCancel": "Annuler",
  "@resetCancel": {
    "description": "Backs out of the reset. Must land on the failure screen, never a blank route."
  },
  "resetContinue": "Continuer",
  "@resetContinue": {
    "description": "Advances to the hold-to-confirm step. Not the destructive action itself."
  },
  "resetHoldTitle": "Maintenez pour supprimer",
  "@resetHoldTitle": {
    "description": "Title of the second reset step."
  },
  "resetHoldInstruction": "Appuyez et maintenez pendant 3 secondes.",
  "@resetHoldInstruction": {
    "description": "A press-and-hold rather than a typed confirmation word. Typing a word on a phone keyboard, in a second script, one-handed, while holding a parcel is the wrong interaction here. A hold is language-neutral, impossible to trigger by muscle memory, and works with one thumb."
  },
  "resetHoldAction": "Maintenir pour supprimer définitivement",
  "@resetHoldAction": {
    "description": "The confirm control says what it does. Never 'OK' or 'Confirmer' — the label is the last thing between the driver and permanent loss."
  },
  "resetDoneTitle": "L'application a redémarré à zéro",
  "@resetDoneTitle": {
    "description": "Shown after a completed reset. Dropping silently into an empty app would read as another failure."
  },
  "resetDoneBody": "Les anciennes données ont été supprimées. Vous pouvez commencer une nouvelle journée.",
  "@resetDoneBody": {
    "description": "Confirms what happened and that the app is usable."
  },
  "resetDoneAction": "Commencer",
  "@resetDoneAction": {
    "description": "Leaves the reset flow into normal startup. The only way off this screen — the reset flow behind it is cleared, since returning would offer to destroy data that no longer exists."
  },
  "customersSearchHint": "Rechercher un client",
